Thanks. (That's why the latter is an option.) I just corrected some
bugs[1] and added another option:

P - Items just Picked up

which selects all items from the last pick up operation. Handy for
moving around stuff and not messing up one's permament inventory. Was a
bit crazy to implement w/o breaking save/bones compatibility. Of course,
for the same reason, it's not persistent--if you save and restore, the
just-picked-up list will be empty (and thus this choice will not appear).

For the latter to take effect, one needs to #define ITEMCAT_JP in
addition to ITEMCAT in config.h.

If you would like to try it, the new diff is at:

<http://home.in.tum.de/~traykovs/nethack/itemcat_jp-342.diff>

___
[1] namely that the choices appeared where they shouldn't -- on the
capital-I inventory listing, where one ends up with an empty list. Also
some additonal rustproofing cleverness.

